},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.6.stable, 4.7.dev 74de2ec04\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.dev (74de2ec04) - Fedora Linux 43 (KDE Plasma Desktop Edition) on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5090 (nvidia; 580.126.18) - AMD Ryzen 9 9950X3D 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 62.33 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nBaseMaterial3D with inverted depth is always invisible when Proximity Fade is enabled.\n\nBy converting to a ShaderMaterial and adjusting the calculation (replace `proximity_view_pos.z + proximity_fade_distance` with `proximity_view_pos.z - proximity_fade_distance`), you can get the expected appearance:\n\n`master` | Expected appearance\n-|-\n<img width=\"722\" height=\"475\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/49fa7f96-4dda-4e83-a2cd-76f72c6dd3bb\" /> | <img width=\"722\" height=\"475\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6819d5b9-81a1-4530-8ec8-7472a96dd0ab\" />\n\nIn the above screenshot, materials in the back have proximity fade disabled. Materials in the front have proximity fade enabled.\n\nBaseMaterial3D could do this automatically in its shader generation code, so you don't need to convert it to a ShaderMaterial.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a StandardMaterial3D, set its depth mode to **Inverted** and enable **Proximity Fade**.\n- Notice the material always being invisible, even when inside or behind other opaque objects, even if the proximity fade distance is set to `0.01` (the lowest possible value).\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[test_proximity_fade_inverted_depth.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25855385/test_proximity_fade_inverted_depth.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117269/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117269/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}